      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Cpanel::JSON::XS versions from 4.42 before 4.80 for Perl let input chunking change the decoded value of top-level numbers in incr_parse.\n\nallow_nonref is enabled by default and incr_parse inherits it. A top-level number, true, false or null has no closing delimiter, so the incremental parser decodes whatever has arrived. The bytes 12 decode as one value when read together, but as 1 and then 2 when split across two reads.\n\nA peer that can influence read boundaries can change how many messages a stream consumer decodes and what values they carry.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
